v 3
d editanything. Open any text file (.ado, .sthlp, .do, .md, .py, .R, .csv, ...) from Stata
d
d editanything is a one-command replacement for SSC's -adoedit- that works
d on any text file -- not just .ado.  It searches the ado-path, opens in the
d Do-file Editor, Viewer, or your OS default app, and refuses to clobber
d Stata-supplied files (use -replace- to copy them into PERSONAL first).
d
d Supports: .ado .sthlp .hlp .smcl .do .mata .md .markdown .html .htm .tex
d .bib .xml .rst .csv .tsv .txt .raw .log .R .r .py .js .css .sql .sh
d .bat .ps1 .json .yaml .yml .toml .ini .cfg .conf .env -- and any other
d plain-text file.
d
d Requires: Stata 14 or newer
d
d Author: Eric A. Booth
d Support: eric.a.booth@gmail.com
d Distribution-Date: 20260526
d
f editanything.ado
f editanything.sthlp
